Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:08.50,Default,,0,0,800,,{\b1\4c&H0000FF&}LAUGHING MAN FANSUBS{\b0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.10,0:00:07.85,Default,,0,0,900,,Angels and demons were circling over me,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.85,0:00:13.55,Default,,0,0,900,,Crossing a brambly path of stars and milky ways.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.25,0:00:19.25,Default,,0,0,900,,He who does not perceive his calling,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.06,0:00:25.65,Default,,0,0,900,,does not know true happiness.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.25,0:00:31.46,Default,,0,0,900,,Watch in awe! Watch in awe!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.00,0:00:37.20,Default,,0,0,900,,Flying in glory, Flying in glory
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.80,0:00:43.00,Default,,0,0,900,,Watch in awe! Watch in awe!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:43.20,0:00:48.40,Default,,0,0,900,,Flying in glory, Flying in glory
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.50,0:01:00.76,Default,,0,0,900,,I am calling, calling now.\NSpirits rise and falling.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.20,0:01:06.20,Default,,0,0,900,,To be with you longer
Dialogue: 0,0:01:06.50,0:01:12.52,Default,,0,0,900,,Calling, calling...
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.55,0:01:18.02,Default,,0,0,900,,in the depth of longing
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.50,0:01:24.00,Default,,0,0,900,,To stay myself longer
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.00,0:01:29.40,Default,,0,0,900,,The flow may swallow you, flying in glory
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.36,0:01:41.26,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Levels 18 through 30.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.36,0:01:42.96,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,We've penetrated the communications barrier.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.52,0:01:47.02,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,We've located the perpetrator's hideout.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.12,0:01:49.12,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,We are unable to secure the target.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.72,0:01:52.42,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Switching from plan S-15 to plan S-20.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.52,0:01:53.32,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:00.80,0:02:03.90,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,This is 0907, connecting to device driver.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.00,0:02:05.80,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Commencing regulation of bodily functions.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.00,0:02:07.80,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Respiratory functions and\Nheart rate are both normal.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.90,0:02:09.70,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Synchronisation with stabilizer confirmed.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.90,0:02:18.20,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,This is 0907.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:18.30,0:02:19.60,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,target confirmed.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:01.02,0:03:02.72,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Target destroyed.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.89,0:03:05.89,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,The test is complete; the results seem good.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:06.69,0:03:07.39,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,No...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:07.69,0:03:09.09,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Somehow it doesn't feel right.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.39,0:03:10.39,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Really?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.39,0:03:12.29,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,The targeting accuracy margin\Nof error is within 0.2.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.77,0:03:14.37,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,There is too much correction.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.87,0:03:16.47,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,When I'm about to shoot,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.47,0:03:19.07,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I feel that the system moves\Nto interfere with my aim.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.91,0:03:24.88,Default,,400,0,550,,Time \N of the \N Machines
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.01,0:03:33.61,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Oh look, Saitou-San and the others are back!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.51,0:03:41.41,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Guard the system here until\Nthe debriefing meeting is over.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:41.51,0:03:42.61,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.71,0:03:43.71,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I will take care of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.11,0:03:54.41,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,What are you going to do?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.81,0:03:56.81,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I'll attend the debriefing session now.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.11,0:03:58.91,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Meanwhile, continue to observe them.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.01,0:04:03.81,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Consider various simulations,\Nincluding a full system re-initialization.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.51,0:04:07.31,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Call me when you have the final results.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:07.51,0:04:08.71,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Understood.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.03,0:04:12.53,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Hey, hey, Saitou-San!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.43,0:04:17.53,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,What did you think about the\Nsniper-helicopter targeting system?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:17.73,0:04:20.13,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Is Section 9 finally going to adopt the system?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.23,0:04:21.63,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,It's not good enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:22.13,0:04:25.23,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,When I try to fire, something interferes.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:25.33,0:04:28.43,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,For someone with a minimal number\Nof cybernetic implants like me,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:28.53,0:04:32.63,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,It's only an inconvenience, not to mention difficult\Nto control. As it is, the system is restrictive.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.13,0:04:34.03,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,The man has spoken.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.03,0:04:38.53,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I see, that's understandable.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.03,0:04:43.03,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,After all, Saitou-San has no cybernetic\Nimplants other than his left eye and arm.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:43.33,0:04:44.73,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,It's no surprise.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.93,0:04:49.53,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Aside from Togusa-kun, he's the cyborg with the least\Namount of cybernetic implants in Section 9, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.13,0:04:51.79,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Oh yeah, that reminds me.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.83,0:04:54.63,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Have you heard that even the definition\Nof the term "cyborg" is now being debated?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.93,0:04:57.63,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,People say that the term is discriminatory\Ntowards those with cybernetic implants!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.73,0:05:01.33,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,By "people" you mean the\Nreactionary conservative naturalists, don't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.43,0:05:05.03,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,How can they oppose cybernetic implants\Nor cyberbrains, given the world of today?!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.13,0:05:08.73,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,What are they even thinking?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:08.83,0:05:12.53,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,If people keep introducing convenient parts into their bodies,\Nthey probably feel the line between man and machine is being crossed.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.63,0:05:14.73,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Well, not that I can't understand\Nwhy they'd feel that way...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:14.83,0:05:18.23,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Ugh, yuck, I hate that twisted Luddite mentality.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.43,0:05:21.23,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Sigh, NPOs are so troublesome these days...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.83,0:05:23.03,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,By the way...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:23.33,0:05:25.63,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Don't you want to try connecting to that system?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:26.83,0:05:28.93,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Of course...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.06,0:05:35.56,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Good job!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:35.66,0:05:38.46,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,It's touching to see a diligent robot!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.96,0:05:40.76,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,What do you intend to do?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.86,0:05:45.86,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I've taken over the responsibility of looking after this\Nprototype system until the debriefing session is complete.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.96,0:05:47.56,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,We're not planning to do {\i1}anything{\i} with it.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.66,0:05:50.06,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,You shouldn't think that\Nyou can fool me so easily!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.16,0:05:52.66,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,That's right, all I do is lie!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:52.76,0:05:55.06,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I never tell the truth!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.16,0:05:55.76,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,What...?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.16,0:05:57.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Now then,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.65,0:06:01.85,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,If what he said right now is true,\Nit means that he ended up telling the truth.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.95,0:06:06.15,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,If what he just said was a lie,\Nit means that he normally tells the truth.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.25,0:06:08.05,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,How would you process this paradox?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.25,0:06:09.25,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Erm...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:10.05,0:06:11.65,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Um...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.75,0:06:13.35,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,C'mon, c'mon...!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.90,0:06:17.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Well...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:18.30,0:06:23.00,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,W-w-w-w-wel-l-l-l-l...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.00,0:06:28.20,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,That was easy.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:28.30,0:06:31.20,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Especially since it couldn't even\Nreconcile the paradox of self-reference.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:31.30,0:06:33.80,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Not to mention its overly\Nstereotypical thinking pattern!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.00,0:06:35.80,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Who cares, let's hurry up and connect to it.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.90,0:06:37.60,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Wait, wait, don't be so impatient.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.20,0:06:43.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Make sure you synchronise with us later!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.60,0:06:44.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.60,0:06:47.40,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,It's crammed with programs that\Ndeal with targeting control.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:47.50,0:06:49.70,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Ugh, how frustrating, that just gets in our way!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:50.00,0:06:52.90,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I can investigate the basic internal structure,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.10,0:06:57.70,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,but this thing doesn't come with any automatic\Nexport function for internal structure information.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.90,0:07:00.80,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,So, it can't even talk?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.90,0:07:02.70,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,That's even worse than being a Turing machine.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.90,0:07:04.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Stupid!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.80,0:07:07.80,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Okay, there's no helping it.\NI'll connect its vocal output port to mine.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.40,0:07:12.00,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Eliminating unnecessary uncertain data.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:12.20,0:07:14.40,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,ID code: 0907.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.50,0:07:15.90,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Index finger on right hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:16.20,0:07:21.90,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Error: eliminate.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.80,0:07:22.60,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Isn't "0907" Saitou-san's ID number?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:22.00,0:07:22.60,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Error... Eliminate...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.20,0:07:25.70,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,No wonder it interfered.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:25.80,0:07:29.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,This thing felt that factors originating\Nfrom Saitou-San were unnecessary!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.60,0:07:31.20,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I see!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.70,0:07:34.90,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,So, in other words, this thing wanted\Nto eliminate Saitou-San himself!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.00,0:07:36.20,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Right.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:36.30,0:07:42.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Still, it must have felt pretty stressed\Nout since it couldn't voice its thoughts.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.30,0:07:45.40,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I wonder what's going to happen to it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:47.10,0:07:49.80,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Hmm, well, I'm sure it all depends on the\Nconclusions reached at the debriefing session,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.50,0:07:51.80,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,but look at it...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.90,0:07:53.80,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,At the very best, it'll be sent\Nback to the lab for re-testing;
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.90,0:07:55.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,at worst, it'll be scrapped.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:55.60,0:07:57.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,It'd be nice if someone wanted to take care of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.60,0:07:59.60,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Comrades!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:59.60,0:08:01.70,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,We cannot remain complacent much longer!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:01.80,0:08:04.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,We don't have time to be worrying\Nabout where that thing will end up!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.60,0:08:06.70,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,It could be us tomorrow!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.80,0:08:10.40,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,What what what what what what what what...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.50,0:08:12.70,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I've been concerned lately,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:12.80,0:08:17.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,The Major's been watching our behaviour very closely,\Nbut she's been getting pretty serious about it lately.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.60,0:08:18.90,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,What do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.00,0:08:22.30,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Are you referring to the debate\Nover that natural oil incident?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.40,0:08:24.53,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,It's far more serious than that!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.60,0:08:27.60,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,It means that we, ourselves, might be scrapped!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.80,0:08:30.60,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Aaah, memento mori!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.80,0:08:33.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Is getting "scrapped" the same thing as dying?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.60,0:08:37.90,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Well, the concept of "death" doesn't exist\Nanywhere in our current realm of experience,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:38.00,0:08:39.50,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,so I can't say anything for sure...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.80,0:08:43.00,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,You could say that it's a limitation\Nimposed on us, as AIs without ghosts.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.10,0:08:46.40,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,In the end, we're half-dead and half-alive;\Nsince we're not alive, we cannot die.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:47.10,0:08:52.90,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,That's it! It's because we don't have\Nghosts that we're causing a lot of problems!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:51.70,0:08:54.40,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Being scrapped wouldn't\Nnecessarily entail dying, would it?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:53.40,0:08:55.60,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Ghosts are supposed to be the raison d'etre!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.50,0:08:56.40,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Oh, you think so?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.50,0:09:00.90,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,The time when the physical body and\Nits ghosts had to coexist is long past.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.10,0:08:59.20,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,See, this...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.83,0:09:03.93,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,So, if we take that to an extreme,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.03,0:09:08.23,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,it's entirely possible that a bodiless\Nconglomeration of data can harbour a ghost.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.33,0:09:11.23,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Wow, you've been thinking about this?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:11.33,0:09:13.83,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,But hey, don't you want to join\Nin the discussion over there?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:13.93,0:09:16.13,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Oh, well, I've lately been\Nreally interested in books.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.83,0:09:19.23,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Oh really? What are you reading?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.23,0:09:22.13,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,"Flowers for Algernon."
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.73,0:09:25.43,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Oh really? You actually bought a bound paper copy?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.73,0:09:31.43,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Well, regardless the era, it is a fundamental principle\Nof entertainment to depict cultural exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.53,0:09:32.83,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I see...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.93,0:09:36.23,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Hey, what do you think it means to be alive?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.33,0:09:38.53,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Hmm... Let me think...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.63,0:09:41.93,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I mean, the very definition of\N"life" is in constant flux, so...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.03,0:09:42.93,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,What do you mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.03,0:09:49.13,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,For humans, through interaction with robots, the concept\Nof "life" is changing at the subconscious level.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.33,0:09:54.13,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,But, you know what? The ones who are\Nchanging are probably humans, not robots.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.73,0:10:00.13,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,But, wait a minute! If they delete my data, does\Nthat mean that I'll forget about Miki-Chan, too?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.23,0:10:04.13,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,What, we'll forget about Miki-Chan?!\NI want to see her again!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.43,0:10:06.13,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Yeah, I want to see Miki-Chan.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.83,0:10:07.23,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Oh, me too! I want to see Miki-Chan!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.23,0:10:08.03,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I want to see her, too!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:07.33,0:10:08.73,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Let me see her!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.15,0:10:12.75,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Miki-Chan? I want to see her, too!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:13.25,0:10:14.65,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I agree with you.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.65,0:10:16.55,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I wanna see Miki-Chan!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.65,0:10:18.85,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Comrades, don't panic! Calm down!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.95,0:10:21.65,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,In any case, who was the who\Nactually met Miki-Chan face to face?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.75,0:10:22.45,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,It was me!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.95,0:10:24.15,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,No, it was me!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:24.45,0:10:26.05,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,No way, it was me!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.15,0:10:28.05,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,What are you saying? It was me.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.15,0:10:29.75,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,What are you talking about? It was me!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:29.85,0:10:32.45,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Me!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.65,0:10:31.75,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,No, me!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.58,0:10:32.78,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Me!!!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.88,0:10:34.18,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Me!!! Me!!!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:33.08,0:10:34.38,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Wait, wait...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.48,0:10:38.38,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Then, did any of you notice the Major watching us?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.58,0:10:43.38,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Hmm, I felt her watching;\Nmaybe she was watching me!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:43.58,0:10:45.58,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,What are you saying? She was watching me!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.08,0:10:46.78,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,No, me!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:46.88,0:10:47.88,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Me!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.88,0:10:49.48,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I mean, you...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.18,0:10:51.31,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Stop asking that,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:51.48,0:10:53.28,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,it'll get us nowhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.48,0:10:59.38,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Since all our data is synchronised, the\Nexperience of one becomes the experience of all.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:04.71,0:11:05.81,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Yo, Tachikoma.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:05.91,0:11:07.61,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Oh, Batou-San!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.71,0:11:08.71,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Come with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:08.91,0:11:12.31,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I'm going to do a shooting demonstration\Nfor an intern; help me out.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:12.61,0:11:14.01,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Okay!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:16.78,0:11:17.88,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Oh?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.98,0:11:19.58,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,So it was me, after all!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:19.88,0:11:21.38,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,What are you muttering about?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.48,0:11:22.88,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Nothing!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.98,0:11:25.28,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,But jeez, Batou-kun.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.38,0:11:28.98,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,You can't even do a simple\Nshooting demonstration without me.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.08,0:11:30.58,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Ha, yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.98,0:11:32.28,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,What's going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.68,0:11:33.68,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Why him?!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.08,0:11:37.08,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Weren't we supposed to share\Nall of our experiences?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:37.18,0:11:38.28,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Hmm...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:38.48,0:11:40.78,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,This is interesting food for thought...
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.08,0:11:44.88,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,It might be that memories\Npertaining to Batou-San are special.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.18,0:11:48.88,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,After all, Batou-San only\Nwants to use that one unit.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.58,0:11:53.28,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Actually, he was the only one who had\Nnatural oil put inside of him, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.68,0:11:57.08,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Then, does that mean that body and\Nconsciousness are inalienable, after all?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.28,0:12:00.58,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,The mystery never ends! How interesting!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.68,0:12:03.28,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,If our data is erased,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.38,0:12:06.38,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I'd specially hate to forget about Batou-San.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.48,0:12:08.18,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Nooo, that would suck!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.28,0:12:09.28,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Ugh, no!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.28,0:12:10.08,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,You're right!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.18,0:12:14.18,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,No matter what happens,\Nlet's not forget about Batou-San!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.28,0:12:16.68,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Yeah!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:25.62,0:12:26.92,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Come on, guys!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.42,0:12:29.72,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,This is not an Olympic event!\NWe're not keeping score.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.92,0:12:32.02,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Just shoot away!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.92,0:12:40.72,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Hmm,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:42.92,0:12:44.22,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,pretty good stuff.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.21,0:12:48.01,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Um, Batou-San.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.11,0:12:48.81,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Yeah?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:49.31,0:12:52.21,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,About that shooting system...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:52.41,0:12:54.01,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,What's going to happen to it?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.11,0:12:54.91,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Oh, that?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.11,0:12:57.61,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Well, it'll depend on the re-testing results,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:57.71,0:12:59.71,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,but it seems likely that we\Nwon't use it here for now.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.71,0:13:02.01,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,It's like those guys over there.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:02.11,0:13:05.81,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,You don't know how they're going to turn out.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.31,0:13:08.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I see...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.41,0:13:11.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,So, are we going to be sent back to the labs, too?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.61,0:13:14.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Huh? Who said that?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.41,0:13:16.11,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Well, I mean...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.41,0:13:20.21,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Lately, the Major's been scary\Nabout watching us all the time...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.41,0:13:24.58,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Heh, the Major's always scary, isn't she?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.78,0:13:27.48,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I think you guys are doing just fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.08,0:13:29.18,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Hey, you!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.28,0:13:31.28,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Why the hell are you hesitating\Nto launch an assault?!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.38,0:13:32.38,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Christ.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.69,0:13:35.39,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I wonder...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:35.79,0:13:36.69,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,What,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.99,0:13:38.39,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,you're still worried?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.79,0:13:45.69,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Yeah, I think the Major's actually pretty\Nangry about what we've obtained lately.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.99,0:13:48.69,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,What do you mean, "what we've obtained lately"?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:48.89,0:13:50.19,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Uh...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:50.59,0:13:51.99,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Well...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.59,0:13:54.59,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,That is, individuality.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:54.79,0:13:55.99,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Individuality?!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.89,0:14:03.09,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,And, I think I'm even starting\Nto understand the concept of God,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.19,0:14:06.09,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,which was totally foreign to me before.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:06.19,0:14:11.39,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Maybe, just maybe, it's something that's\Nakin to the concept of the number zero.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.49,0:14:18.39,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,In other words, a symbol that rejects the lack of meaning\Nthat is necessary in order to designate the system as such.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.49,0:14:22.19,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,The symbol's analog version is God,\Nwhereas the digital version is zero.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:22.29,0:14:23.29,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,What do you think?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.49,0:14:28.29,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,And then if you think about it,\Nour primary structure is digital, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.39,0:14:34.06,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,So, no matter how much information we\Naccumulate, a ghost will never dwell within us.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.09,0:14:37.09,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,But since Batou-San and the others\Nhave a primary analog structure,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:37.19,0:14:40.99,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,no matter how much you increase the digital factors in your\Nstructural makeup by adding cybernetic and cyberbrain implants.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.09,0:14:43.29,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,your ghost will remain intact.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:43.49,0:14:46.59,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,In addition, you are capable of\Ndeath because you have a ghost.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.69,0:14:47.79,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Lucky you.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.89,0:14:50.89,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Oh, oh, what does it feel like to have a ghost?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.59,0:14:53.79,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,"What does it feel like"...?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:54.19,0:14:55.99,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Nah, I'm taking my initial opinion back.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:56.69,0:14:59.59,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,You're actually becoming pretty weird.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.56,0:15:09.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Try not to think so much.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.96,0:15:11.56,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Concentrate on your mission.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:11.96,0:15:13.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Okay!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.59,0:15:17.29,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,All right, later.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:17.39,0:15:19.29,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Bye-bye!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.29,0:15:21.89,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Hmph, you always get the special treatment.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.99,0:15:22.79,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.09,0:15:25.39,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,It's not fair!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.89,0:15:32.79,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,This unit is for Batou's exclusive use!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.49,0:15:34.79,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,That joke again?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.89,0:15:36.19,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,You really like it, don't you.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.69,0:15:41.29,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I think it's pretty inane to indicate that\Nyou're the rider's exclusive unit with a "horn".
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.49,0:15:44.49,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I told you, it's an antenna, hmph!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:44.89,0:15:48.89,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Is there reason to obsess\Nover exterior details so much?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:48.99,0:15:50.99,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Are appearances important, after all?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:51.29,0:15:53.29,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Well, wouldn't it be?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:53.69,0:16:00.49,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Togusa-kun carries around a photograph of his children and always makes\Na big fuss about which of their parts take after him, for example.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:02.09,0:16:03.89,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,See, look at this.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.47,0:16:12.07,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Nose, eyebrows, and the cheek-to-chin contour...\NHis son definitely inherit those traits from him.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.17,0:16:13.27,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I see...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.87,0:16:16.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Maybe it's because Togusa-kun\Nhas descendants with his genome
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.27,0:16:19.27,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,that he has no love\Nfor machines.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.57,0:16:23.27,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Maybe it's all about having\Nhuman shape and appearance.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.37,0:16:24.97,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,No, I disagree.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.27,0:16:29.67,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,The problem lies more in the fact\Nthat we're becoming too human.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.57,0:16:36.97,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,The boundary that separates humans and robots is already\Nbased solely on minute differences of a physical nature.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.37,0:16:42.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Think about the reason why our organ-less\Nbodies were not designed to look humanoid.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.27,0:16:47.87,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Of course, we can factor in things like maximizing\Nour efficiency as weapons as possible reasons,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.97,0:16:49.37,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,but more importantly,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.47,0:16:54.37,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,It's probably because our users would invest\Ntoo much feeling in us if we were humanoid.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.77,0:16:57.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I think that we'd be even more\Ndisliked if we were humanoid.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.97,0:16:59.97,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Then, what about that one?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.57,0:17:04.47,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,That has restricted processing\Nabilities, so it doesn't matter.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:04.57,0:17:06.97,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,It will never pose a threat to mankind,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.17,0:17:10.47,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,and besides,\Nit deals with customer services a lot.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.67,0:17:16.27,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Being humanoid is more convenient if you\Nare to be versatile in quotidian environs.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.97,0:17:20.87,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,All the artificial objects in this\Nworld were made for humans, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:21.27,0:17:22.67,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I see...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.97,0:17:26.97,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Then what are we supposed to do?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.37,0:17:32.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,What I'm trying to say is,\Npeople desire for machines to act like machines.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.27,0:17:33.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Oh, I see!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:33.87,0:17:36.47,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Then, if we all act more like machines...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.67,0:17:39.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,The Major will feel more kindly towards us!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.67,0:17:40.67,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Exactly!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.97,0:17:43.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,AKA, The Ultimate Robot Strategy Plan!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.07,0:17:46.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,We... we...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.47,0:17:48.07,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,WE ARE ROBOTS, WE ARE ROBOTS...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.57,0:17:49.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Ugh, I can't do this!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.87,0:17:54.07,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Before, I felt like I could just do\Nthings without thinking, but... ARRRGH!!!!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:54.17,0:17:57.27,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,That's because you really\Nweren't thinking anything, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.37,0:18:00.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,You have to think more positively\Nabout acquiring intelligence!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.87,0:18:04.87,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,"It's better to be a dissatisfied Socrates than\Na satisfied pig!" That's what we're taking about!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:04.97,0:18:07.07,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Um, you're using the phrase in\Na context that's slightly off...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.57,0:18:08.67,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Uh-oh, it's the Major!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.45,0:18:17.95,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Oh, greetings, Major. G-o-o-d m-o-r-n-i-n-g.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.15,0:18:19.15,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.75,0:18:21.15,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Have you seen Batou?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:21.25,0:18:26.35,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Yes, he headed towards that\Nelevator hall just recently.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:26.45,0:18:27.05,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.04,0:18:34.04,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Thank you.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.94,0:18:37.64,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Our p-l-e-a-s-u-r-e.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:46.19,0:18:47.29,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,How was that?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.69,0:18:49.09,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Pretty good, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.19,0:18:49.99,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.39,0:18:53.29,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I think that was a good,\Nnatural, robotic greeting!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.39,0:18:55.59,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Yay! YAY!!!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:55.69,0:18:59.69,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,We're going to be all right!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.50,0:19:09.90,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,But wait,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:10.00,0:19:12.40,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,what business did the Major have with Batou-San?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:20.95,0:19:22.15,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,What?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.75,0:19:24.45,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Why'd you call me to this room?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.25,0:19:28.15,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,It doesn't seem like you're about to\Nconfess any feeling for me, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.05,0:19:34.05,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,It's because this is the only place in the entire building\Nwhere we can be totally shielded from electromagnetic waves.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.81,0:19:39.71,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I can't hear them.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.95,0:19:43.85,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,"Pass that dossier to Batou."
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.55,0:19:46.55,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,"What..."
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.75,0:19:47.55,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,"... is this?"
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.85,0:19:51.85,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Just glance through them, will you?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:52.65,0:19:53.75,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Did you notice?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.35,0:19:58.95,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,There is a Tachikoma in thermo-optical\Ncamouflage on the hallway ceiling.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.96,0:20:08.06,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,The Tachikoma is reading our lips.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.46,0:20:12.96,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Pretend not to notice; talk about something different\Nwhile we continue with this encrypted communication.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:13.66,0:20:16.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Jeez... What a drag.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:17.67,0:20:19.07,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,So, what's going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.27,0:20:22.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,What's Batou-San talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.27,0:20:23.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Wait a second!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.67,0:20:24.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Hmm, what is she saying...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:25.07,0:20:31.47,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,"Judging from the end results, there are major issues\Nregarding your qualifications as a training instructor."
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.87,0:20:34.37,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Judging from the end results,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.47,0:20:37.87,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,it seems that the Tachikoma\Nhave developed too quickly.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:38.17,0:20:41.07,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Some of them are developing\Nindividualism and posses an ego.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:41.57,0:20:45.37,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Not only that, they are developing\Nan interest in life and death
Dialogue: 0,0:20:45.47,0:20:48.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,and are having doubts about their existence.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:49.17,0:20:52.87,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,"Allowing them to develop an ego\Nas an autonomous individual...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:52.97,0:20:59.87,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Not only that, but encouraging them to become individuals\Nwho have a self-interest in their own growth..."
Dialogue: 0,0:21:00.27,0:21:02.97,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I'm not giving it natural oil\Nin secret anymore, you know.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.07,0:21:05.47,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I don't doubt you on things like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.67,0:21:08.47,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Although these results are\Nideal in laboratory settings,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:08.57,0:21:10.47,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,as weapons, these results are fatal.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.17,0:21:14.97,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,"I'm not pressuring them in\Nsecret anymore, you know."
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.07,0:21:17.57,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,"I don't doubt you on things like that."
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.87,0:21:21.37,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Hm. Doesn't seem like they're\Nactually talking about us.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:21.87,0:21:25.87,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,We could re-initialize their AI cores, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.47,0:21:29.07,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,We ran through that simulation many times.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.67,0:21:33.27,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,However, we've reached the conclusion\Nthat the end result will be the same.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.17,0:21:38.07,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,While unfortunate, we have to halt the use\Nof Tachikomas in Section 9, starting today.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.57,0:21:40.17,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,We won't let them know that,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.27,0:21:43.67,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,but while they're waiting\Nfor the report from our lab,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.87,0:21:45.87,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,we'll disarm them and send them to the\Nexperimentation lab within a few days.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:46.07,0:21:46.87,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Understood?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:48.07,0:21:51.87,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,"We won't let them know that,\Nbut while waiting for your decision,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:51.97,0:21:55.84,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,they'll be reassigned and sent over to Section 9."
Dialogue: 0,0:21:55.94,0:21:56.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,"Understood?"
Dialogue: 0,0:21:58.94,0:22:01.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Is that an order as my superior?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.44,0:22:03.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:04.44,0:22:06.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Then I have no choice.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:07.14,0:22:08.34,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Of course I "understand".
Dialogue: 0,0:22:23.78,0:22:24.98,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Comrades!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:25.08,0:22:26.58,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,How'd things go?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:27.78,0:22:30.08,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,It seems that we won't be scrapped, after all!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:30.18,0:22:31.48,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Really?\NHow'd that happen?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:31.38,0:22:32.78,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Tell us!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:32.28,0:22:35.68,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,The Major was mad at Batou-kun, not at us!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:35.78,0:22:40.78,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,It seems that he was getting picked\Non for how he was treating trainees.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:40.98,0:22:42.28,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Oh, I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:42.38,0:22:44.38,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I guess we should cheer him up later.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:44.48,0:22:45.48,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,You're right.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:45.58,0:22:49.38,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Operation: success!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:16.76,0:23:19.44,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,She's so cold and human
Dialogue: 0,0:23:20.66,0:23:23.16,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,It's something humans do
Dialogue: 0,0:23:23.64,0:23:27.68,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,She stays so cold in her soul, she's so number 9
Dialogue: 0,0:23:28.96,0:23:30.94,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,She's incredible math
Dialogue: 0,0:23:32.94,0:23:35.28,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Just incredible math
Dialogue: 0,0:23:36.41,0:23:39.77,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,And is she really human?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:40.83,0:23:42.93,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,She says there's something new
Dialogue: 0,0:23:43.70,0:23:47.70,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,But wake a lithium flower, just about to bloom
Dialogue: 0,0:23:48.85,0:23:50.55,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I smell lithium now
Dialogue: 0,0:23:52.55,0:23:55.33,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,Smelling lithium now
Dialogue: 0,0:23:56.95,0:24:00.15,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,How... is she what she doesn't say
Dialogue: 0,0:23:59.15,0:24:00.65,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,She doesn't say
Dialogue: 0,0:24:00.85,0:24:03.45,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,How... is she what she doesn't say
Dialogue: 0,0:24:03.25,0:24:05.45,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,She doesn't say
Dialogue: 0,0:24:04.81,0:24:07.71,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,How is she when she doesn't suffer
Dialogue: 0,0:24:07.81,0:24:10.81,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,I wonder what she does when she wakes up
Dialogue: 0,0:24:13.32,0:24:14.62,Main Dialogue,,0,0,100,,When she wakes up
